  "updated_H5_classification": "two_plant_routes_supported_general_global_isolation_pollen_limitation_association_supported_but_predeclared_north_tropical_service_branching_not_supported_named_architecture_support_limited_exact_island_identity_nonidentifiable",
  "updated_H5_statement": "Across the full georeferenced GloPL sampling frame, experimental pollen limitation increases with distance from the seeded major continental landmasses under the frozen global model, and a post-hoc shape audit indicates that the association continues within offshore sites rather than being only a mainland-versus-offshore level shift. However, the predeclared northern-midlatitude versus tropical service-gradient prediction is not supported and the tropical gradient is point-estimated as stronger, not weaker. The strict exact-island area-and-climate-adjusted subset remains imprecise and unsupported. Thus a broad isolation-associated pollen-limitation relationship is supported, but it does not identify the context-specific common upstream mechanism for the Chapter 1 floral/reproductive H2 branching.",
